    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287-a3">

                <pb facs="0406" n="318" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg318"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Brittain to Mr.
                            Dodge.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kehl</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1903-12-26"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">December 26,
                    1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In response to your letter of the 19th
                    instant I herewith return the citizenship papers of Emil Vibert, and beg to
                    state that he was born February 1, 1874, and emigrated to the United States in
                    1886, and has never returned to Germany.</p>
                <p>He was born in St. Quirin, Lorraine, near Saarburg.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph I.
                    Brittain.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
